When you enter the [[ON:Circus of Cheerful Slaughter (place)|Circus of Cheerful Slaughter]], Sheogorath will have you participate in his play ''[[Online:The Folly of Isolation|The Folly of Isolation]]''. While Shalidor does not appear in the realm itself, there will be "interludes" which show fragments of Shalidor's life.

In the first scene a spectral Shalidor is seen speaking to his adepts in the ruins of a hall: 
:'''Arch-Mage Shalidor:''' ''"The world is a cruel place, my assistants. Mages are envied their power, and reviled for using it. We must have a place where we can study in seclusion. A place where all Mages can be safe."''

On the path to Daggerwaymore, Shalidor will appear a few times. The first time he is celebrating his success:
:'''Arch-Mage Shalidor:''' ''"{{sic|Ulfsild the Evergreen|Ulfsild. Her title was added in the subtitles with update 42, but the audio is still the original}}, I did it! I have created a sanctuary, a retreat that will endure for eons! I shall call it … Eyevea!"''

Shortly after you move forward, he will be cursing at Sheogorath:
:'''Arch-Mage Shalidor:''' ''"Sheogorath! You bastard, the Folium Discognitum wasn't worth an island! I'll get Eyevea back, even if it takes three lifetimes!"''

Shalidor appears again at a campfire, this time he is drunk and angry:
:'''Arch-Mage Shalidor:''' ''"Damn the Mad God. Damn Ulfsild! Damn the lot of them!"''
:'''Arch-Mage Shalidor:''' ''"They'll see … they'll all see. Archmage Shalidor's name will ring across history!"''

[[File:ON-quest-Circus of Cheerful Slaughter 07.jpg|thumb|Ulfsild and Shalidor]]
In the final scene on the path, Shalidor will be writing notes while his wife Ulfsild attempts to get his attention:
:'''Ulfsild the Evergreen''': ''"Shalidor! Eyevea is lost … you're obsessed! Can you even hear me?"''
:<Shalidor continues to write, making no sign that he heard her.>
