At this point Sheogorath will appear on the path before you and Shalidor will turn around to face him.
:'''Sheogorath''': ''"Not so fast there, Shalidor. Only invited guests at the Chateau. We have standards, you know."''
:'''Arch-Mage Shalidor''': ''"Damn you, Mad God!"''
:'''Sheogorath''': ''"Don't let the door hit you on the way out, Shally."''
:<Sheogorath waves his hand at Shalidor.>
:'''Sheogorath''': ''"Annnd … off you go!"''
:<Shalidor disappears and Sheogorath focuses on you.>
:'''Sheogorath''': ''"Just the two of us. Now we can talk in peace."''

Though Shalidor is no longer physically there, he is able to perceive what is happening and will offer you advice and commentary about your trials in the Chateau.

When you arrive in the Chateau's guesthouse, you will need to evict one of the guests. Shalidor is able to give some advice before Sheogorath chimes in.
:'''Arch-Mage Shalidor''': ''"Be wary. Talk to these "guests" carefully before you try to throw anyone out."''
:'''Sheogorath''': ''"I can hear you, Shally! Don't bother my guests!"''
:'''Arch-Mage Shalidor''': ''"You're the only one that thinks you're funny, Mad God!"''

While navigating the maze, Sheogorath and Shalidor can be heard to argue while the latter encourages you.
:'''Arch-Mage Shalidor''': ''"You've faced darkness before, adept. Remember your training."''
:'''Sheogorath''': ''"No cheating, Shalidor! Don't ruin this for me."''

After lighting two of the four braziers:
:'''Arch-Mage Shalidor''': ''"Only two more to go. This trial is child's play."''
:'''Sheogorath''': ''"I'm going to bind you to haunt a little old lady in Wayrest! Does that sound fun, Shally?"''

While exploring the manse you will encounter feral madmen, members of Sheogorath's family. Shalidor pities them while Sheogorath just wonders how Shaidlor keeps getting in to commentate.
:'''Arch-Mage Shalidor''': ''"Those poor souls. Sheogorath's "family.""''
:'''Sheogorath''': ''"How do you keep getting back in here? I blame Haskill."''
:'''Arch-Mage Shalidor''': ''"Apparently, not everything is under your control!"''
:'''Sheogorath''': ''"Not yet, anyway."''

===The Mad God's Bargain===
When Shalidor contacts you again, he will be in a much better mood. He will say:
:''"Adept, good to see you!"''

Speaking to him:
:''"I have great news for you, Adept!"''
:'''What's the news?'''
:''"Valaste has finished final analysis of the tomes! We're ready to get my island back!"''
:'''Where can I find her?'''
{|class=hiddentable
|width=33%|<center>'''{{ESO AD}} Aldmeri Dominion:'''</center>
|width=33%|<center>'''{{ESO DC}} Daggerfall Covenant:'''</center>
|width=33%|<center>'''{{ESO EP}} Ebonheart Pact:'''</center>
|-
|
:''"She's preparing a ritual space at the Rawl'kha Guildhall in Reaper's March. I'll see you there, Adept. We're so close!"''
|
:''"She's preparing a ritual space at the Evermore Guildhall in Bangkorai. I'll see you there, Adept. We're so close!"''
|
:''"She's preparing a ritual space at the Riften Guildhall in The Rift. I'll see you there, Adept. We're so close!"''
|}
:'''You seem excited, Shalidor.'''
:''"Of course! This is what we've worked for, all this time. Putting up with the mocking and insults, Sheogorath's poor attempts at humor. We'll recover the isle, and the Guild will have a safe haven from the war!"''

When you arrive at the mentioned guildhall, Valaste will have gotten worse. You will then need to place the four books around the ritual circle so Shalidor can appear.
:'''Arch-Mage Shalidor''': ''"Ahh … the ebb and swell of magicka. How I missed this."''
[[File:ON-quest-The Mad God's Bargain.jpg|thumb|right|Shalidor ready to begin the ritual to bring Eyevea back to Tamriel]]
You can then talk to Shalidor who will be ready to reclaim his island.
:''"We've done it! We're finally ready to take back my island."''
:'''What's the plan?'''
:''"I'll use the combined powers of the books and wrench the isle back to Tamriel. Sheogorath has lost, adept. We're almost there."''
:'''What can we expect on the island?'''
:''"It's a lush place, gorgeous and vibrant. We have guild members poised across Tamriel, ready to join us there. It will be the perfect place for the guild to study in peace. It will be glorious."''
:'''Shalidor, Valaste is not well.'''
:''"I … I know. She's very tired, even worse than before. But she's done masterful work in translating these books. And I'm sure she'll be an asset once we reach the island. She'll have plenty of time to rest soon enough!"''
:'''She's exhausted, and speaking strangely.'''
:''"I suppose she has been garbling her words a bit. I just assumed that it was due to mortal frailty … I sometimes forget how fragile you are. We will watch over her together, my friend."''
:'''But the trials are over, right?'''
:''"I believe so. I'm sure you're as sick of the Mad God's games as I am. <br>Now come. I will perform the ritual and open a portal to our new home."''

He will then begin the ritual.
:<Shalidor holds his hands as if in prayer.>
:'''Arch-Mage Shalidor''': ''"Tomes! Attend me!"''
:<The four tomes then leave their pedestals and whirl around him as he levitates.>
:'''Arch-Mage Shalidor''': ''"Now … I reclaim what was taken from me. Eyevea! Hear my call!"''
A blue-green light haze will fill the area as the portal opens. Shalidor senses something after the portal is created.
:'''Arch-Mage Shalidor''': ''"Something is wrong. I sense … Adept, Valaste. Follow me!"''

When you arrive on Eyevea, you will find various Daedra roaming the island. An angry Shalidor can be found in front of a smoking corpse of a Daedroth.
:''"Damn me for a fool! Why did I trust that madman?"''
:'''What do you mean?'''
:''"What do I mean? Look at this place! The island is overrun with Daedra. Sheogorath has given us the apple, but it's riddled with worms."''
:'''What do we do?'''
:''"There's a grand hall in the center of the island. We'll be able to survey the situation better from that vantage point. You and Valaste make your way up this path. I'll meet you there."''
:'''See you there.'''

Shalidor will then leave you as you and Valaste make your way to the hall. However, when you arrive at the hall, Shalidor will be shouting at Sheogorath who is standing in front of the hall's entrance which has a glowing purple ward on it.
:'''Arch-Mage Shalidor:''' ''"This is not what we agreed to, Mad God! Leave this place."''
:'''Sheogorath''': ''"Careful, mage. Remember who you're talking to."''
:<Sheogorath notices you and binds Shalidor in place with butterflies.>
:'''Sheogorath''': ''"Our mortal friend has arrived! Be quiet now, Shally. Adults talking."''

After you speak with Sheogorath who will make dark hints about Valaste's state and explain how to close the daedra portal, he will leave and Shalidor will freed. You can then talk to Shalidor to explain what you heard.
:''"Damn it. What was I thinking, attacking the Prince of Madness?"''
:'''Sheogorath said something about Valaste, and the curse he placed on the books?'''
:''"Wait, adept … you're not making sense. What do you mean? Sheogorath put that curse on those books to slow us down, make the task more time-consuming."''
:'''He said he knew there were only a few people in the guild that could translate the books.'''
:''"Then … the curse was meant to put the books in front of Valaste. She was meant to read them. Adept, this is very worrying. But we need to deal with this after the island is safe."''
:'''What about Valaste?'''
:''"She'll be with you! She'll be fine for the moment. <br>Valaste, go with our friend here to close the portals. The adept will keep you safe."''
:'''What will you be doing?'''
:''"Sheogorath left a powerful ward on this building. I'll need a few moments to crack it open. Go! I should be done here by the time you return."''
:'''We'll see it done.'''

He will then get to work:
:'''Arch-Mage Shalidor:''' ''"Go! Close the portals! I will see this done."''

Speaking to him while he's trying to open the door:
:''"I'll keep working to open this door.<br>Go close the portals. Hurry!"''

Once you start placing the crystals:
:''"They're all closed? Good, now place the crystals and the barrier should fade."''

Once you have destroyed the crystals and return to Shalidor, he will have managed to make a hole in the wards.
:''"Thanks to you, the island is ours! Now you'll just need to claim the hall and kick Sheogorath back to the Shivering Isles."''
:'''I'll need to claim the hall? What about you and Valaste?'''
:''"I've put a crack in his ward, but no more. The Mad God's power is formidible, even here. You and Valaste may enter. I may not. Just make sure to watch after her. I can see the state she's in."''
:'''As we dealt with the portals, she began to become more agitated. Raving.'''
:''"I fear the Mad God may have gotten the better of us. But perhaps something can be done. Go inside, deal with Sheogorath. We've come too far to be put off by his tricks now."''
:'''I'll take care of him.'''

Shalidor will attack the ward a final time to break it:
:'''Arch-Mage Shalidor''': ''"You can do this adept. You've proven yourself, that you're up to this. Good luck!"''
:<Once the door is unlocked, Valaste will run in ahead of you.>
:'''Valaste''': ''"I can hear him! I'm coming Uncle Sheo!"''

If you speak with him before entering the hall.
:''"Don't worry. I'll speak with her. Go, face Sheogorath. You'll do her more good in there than out here."''

When you enter the hall, you will be forced to fight Haskill. Once you have won, Shalidor will arrive, and you can watch the confrontation. However, the Mad God has his eyes fixed on someone else.
:'''Arch-Mage Shalidor:''' ''"Enough with the games, Sheogorath. Are you going to relinquish the island to us or not?"''
:'''Sheogorath''': ''"All right, all right. Settle down. I'll just gather my things and go. Valaste! Dearie, why don't you come over here?"''
:<Valaste will run into the room.>
:'''Valaste''': ''"Uncle Sheo? Are we going somewhere?"''
:'''Sheogorath''': ''"Yes, little one. You're coming with me. Home to the Shivering Isles! Won't that be nice?"''
:'''Arch-Mage Shalidor:''' ''"Mad God, stay back! Valaste isn't yours to take!"''
:'''Sheogorath''': ''"Isn't she though? I can see it on her face, smell it in the air. She's crazy, mad, a lunatic. All that time with Uncle Sheo's stories and she's got the urge to visit the Isles. My Shivering Isles."''
:'''Valaste''': ''"I do! I want to go with Uncle Sheo! He's got the butterflies! I love butterflies!"''
:'''Sheogorath''': ''"Hmm, this is a conundrum. A riddle, a … choice. I tell you what, mortal. Why don't we let you decide? Should Valaste stay? Or come with me to the dear old Isles?"''
:'''Arch-Mage Shalidor:''' ''"And if the adept decides she goes with you?"''
:'''Sheogorath''': ''"Well, as it happens I have one more book here. I'd give it to you in exchange for Valaste. It's called … the Folium Discognitum."''
:'''Arch-Mage Shalidor:''' ''"Sheogorath, you bastard! You'd throw the Folium back in my face, after all these years?"''
:'''Sheogorath''': ''"Wrote it myself, it's a delightful little artifact. It imbues the reader with the knowledge of madmen! It's very powerful … worth oh, four or five of those [[Online:Skyshards|skyshard]] things you adventurers are always looking for."''
:'''Sheogorath''': ''"So! Valaste stays and I cure her. Or … she goes with me and you, my little mortal, become much more powerful. Your choice!"''

With this important decision pending, you have the option of speaking with Valaste and Shalidor before answering Sheogorath.
:''"Adept, you cannot listen to this offer. This is the exact same offer Sheogorath made me when I first lost Eyevea!"''
:'''What happened?'''
:''"Life for an Arch-Mage is measured in decades, not years. The rituals I performed extended my life, allowed me to continue my work … but eventually even I began to slow down."''
:'''And he offered you this Folium?'''
:''"I began work on a powerful artifact, a key to the inner workings of life itself. Glamoril … but that's neither here nor there. The point is I reached a critical juncture where even my knowledge and power failed me. I needed more."''
:'''And in the bargain, you lost Eyevea.'''
:''"Yes. I'd read all of the Accords of Madness. I knew the lessons of King {{Sic|Lyrandir|Lyandir}}, Leopold Arsenault, Darius Shano … and still I failed. Don't make the mistakes we did, adept. Reject this madman's offer."''

Speaking to him again before a decision to be made:
:''"Remember what I said, adept. Don't make the same mistake I did. A woman's life isn't worth personal power."''

If you decided save Valaste, Sheogorath will announce your choice:
:'''Sheogorath''': ''"The mortal's decided to let Valaste stay! So, this is where I say my goodbyes. Mortal, nice working with you! Shalidor … never change."''
:<Sheogorath points his finger at Valaste and a stream of magenta light flows out of her.>
:'''Sheogorath''': ''"Valaste … sorry dear. Say goodbye to the little dreamlings!"''
:<The beam of energy stops and Valaste looks exhausted.>
:'''Sheogorath''': ''"The Prince of Madness doesn't stay where he's not wanted … heh, except when he does. But in this case, he doesn't! Until next time, Magelings!"''
:<Sheogorath and Haskill leave.>
:'''Valaste''': ''"It's like … it's like a fog has lifted from inside my mind. Adept, I don't know what to say. You've saved me from a fate worse than death."''
:'''Arch-Mage Shalidor:''' ''"Valaste … are you?"''
:'''Valaste''': ''"Yes, I'm … all right, Shalidor. I'm myself again."''

Speaking with Shalidor before checking on Valaste:
:''"We've done it. The island is ours. We've won!"''

Once you have spoken with Valaste, Shalidor will head outside the hall:
:'''Arch-Mage Shalidor:''' ''"I can't stay in here, adept. Let us speak some more outside."''

However, if you decided take the Folium Discognitum, you will need to speak with Sheogorath again. He will then announce your choice to the room. Shalidor can only look on in dismay while Sheogorath takes Valaste away.
:'''Sheogorath''': ''"The mortal's decided to let Valaste go with me! Valaste, dearie, come on over. You're coming with Uncle Sheo."''
:'''Valaste''': ''"Yay! The butterflies! I love to watch them flutter!"''
:'''Arch-Mage Shalidor:''' ''"He's … he's won again. Please don't take her, Mad God!"''
:'''Sheogorath''': ''"Oh, don't worry, she's in good hands! And this is where I say my farewells. Mortal, nice working with you! Shalidor … never change. Say goodbye, dearie."''
:'''Valaste''': ''"Goodbye! I'll miss you!"''
:'''Sheogorath''': ''"Until next time, Magelings!"''
:<Sheogorath, Haskill and Valaste leave in purple light. Shalidor doesn't want to stay either.>
:'''Arch-Mage Shalidor:''' ''"I can't stay in here, adept. Let us speak some more outside."''
[[File:ON-quest-The Arch-Mage's Boon.jpg|thumb|right|Shalidor bestows the Eidetic Memory]]

===The Arch-Mage's Boon===
After you have won back Eyevea, and help decide Valaste's fate, Shalidor will ask you to meet him outside:
:'''Arch-Mage Shalidor ''': ''"I can't stay in here, adept. Let us speak some more outside."''

Once outside, he will ask you to approach him:
:'''Arch-Mage Shalidor ''': ''"Come here, Adept. I have something for you."''

Shalidor will have special gift to give you, though his words will depend on the choice you made concerning Valaste verses Power:
{|class=hiddentable
|width=50%|<center>'''You chose to save Valaste:'''</center>
|width=50%|<center>'''You chose more [[ON:Skill Points|Power]]:'''</center>
|-
|
:''"Adept. You've done so much for the Guild. I couldn't let you leave without a final gift. This old Arch-Mage has a spell he's been saving just for you."''
:'''A gift?
:''"During my time on Tamriel, I developed a very useful spell. A memory charm of sorts. Rather than wasting my time puttering around in libraries trying to find a book, the spell allows me to recall it instantly.<br>If you'll allow me?"''
:'''Go ahead, Shalidor.'''

He will then begin the ritual:
:'''Arch-Mage Shalidor ''': ''"Just need a moment to prepare … this spell has proven very handy. Once saved my life when I came up against a rhyming spirit. She demanded every answer to her questions be answered with a couplet."''

Shalidor will channel the magic for a few moments:
:'''Arch-Mage Shalidor ''':''"There we go. I'm ready. Call it "Shalidor's Library of the Mind." Hah!"''

You can then talk with him when you are ready:
:''"Shor's bones, I can't thank you enough. In time, the body you and Valaste have formed for me will fade. But with this charm, you'll never forget our trials together. I take comfort in that.<br>Are you ready?"''
:'''I'm ready.'''
:''"Then accept the gift of Eidetic Memory. Remember now every tome, every book, every scrap of paper you have ever read.<br>And remember, too, the tale of Eyevea's return to Tamriel, and the story of the Adept who made it happen."''

You will then levitate in the air as you receive the Eidetic Memory ability.
:'''Arch-Mage Shalidor ''': ''"Don't be a stranger, Adept. Eyevea is another home for you, now, as it is for every Mage in Tamriel."''
|
:''"Adept. You've done so much … I thought you were the Guild's future. But I cannot ignore the choice you made concerning Valaste's fate. I would give you a gift. A gift, and a warning."''
:'''A gift?'''
:''"During my time on Tamriel, I developed a very useful spell. A memory charm of sorts. It allows me to recall a book, any moment in time, instantly and without pause. I would ask you to accept it as a gift for your service … and as penance."''
:'''Go ahead, Shalidor.'''

He will then begin the ritual:
:'''Arch-Mage Shalidor ''': ''"Just need a moment to prepare … Adept, I don't blame you for choosing as you did. I made the same choice, years ago. I just hope … I thought you were better than that. Now, I hope you remember the look on her face. For all your years."''

Shalidor will channel the magic for a few moments:
:'''Arch-Mage Shalidor ''': ''"There, I'm ready. Call this "Shalidor's Library of the Mind.""''

You can then talk with him when you are ready:
:''"In time, the body you and Valaste have formed for me will fade. But with this charm, you'll never forget our trials together. The decision you made. I take comfort in that.<br>Are you ready?"''
:'''I'm ready.'''
:''"Then accept the penance of Eidetic Memory. Remember now every tome, every book, every scrap of paper you have ever read.<br>And remember, too, the tale of Eyevea's return to Tamriel, and your role in that tale."''

You will then levitate in the air as you receive the Eidetic Memory ability.
:'''Arch-Mage Shalidor ''': ''"Be sure to come back, Adept. Eyevea is another home for you, now, as it is for every Mage in Tamriel. Valaste would have wanted it this way."''
|}

If you speak with him afterwards, he wish you well regardless of the choice you made: 
:''"Good luck, my friend. Wherever your travels take you next, know that you have all of the Guild at your back."''
<!--"I'll be honest, adept. I can barely stand to look at you. Sending an intelligent woman like Valaste off with that creature. But … I feel honor bound to offer you a final gift."-->

==Skills and Abilities==
When Arch-Mage Shalidor is your follower, he uses the following ability:
;Flare:Basic ranged attack dealing low [[ON:Flame Damage|flame damage]].

==Deprecated Content==
With [[Online:Update 42|Update 42]], the exchange during [[ON:Circus of Cheerful Slaughter|Circus of Cheerful Slaughter]] was changed to better fit the updated backstory as shown in the Scribing questline.

The original scene went as follows:
:'''Ulfsild''': ''"You didn't come home last night. I waited all night for you. Have you been working this entire time?"''
:<Shalidor continues to write, making no sign that he heard her.>
:'''Ulfsild''': ''"Shalidor! Eyevea is lost … you're obsessed! Can you even hear me?"''
:<He continues to write.>
:'''Ulfsild''': ''"I can't do this anymore. You love your spells and scrolls more than you love me. I'm leaving you. Can you hear me now?"''
:<Silence.>
:'''Ulfsild''': ''"Goodbye … you stupid old fool."''
:<Ulfsild disappears, Shalidor stops writing and looks around.>
:'''Arch-Mage Shalidor:''' ''"Ulfie … my love? I swear I just heard you. Where did you go?"''

